SICA accuracy peaks at $T_{\text{ext}} = 0.3$ ($+3.43$\,pp) and exhibits an inverted-U pattern: lower temperatures produce overly deterministic extractions that mirror the trace verbatim, while higher temperatures degrade constraint quality, confirming the default choice.

